 "narrative": "Very good demand for all classes and qualities of hay.  As the drought was severe and hay growth was greatly affected, especially grass hay, there is a much lighter supply of hay across the region.  Corn harvest has finished up, and corn stalk baling resumed this week as the sun and wind have allowed for better conditions to make corn stalk bales.  Usage of bedding has been high already this fall as the big rains in October and subsequent sloppy yard conditions required livestock operators to use quite a bit already.",
